INT. WIRELESS ROOM - STEAMSHIP "MERIDIAN" - NIGHT (1912)

A cramped brass-and-oak cabin. A spark-gap transmitter crackles. A speaking tube hangs by the door.

AGNES FENWICK (20s, wireless operator, ink on her cuffs) taps a key, headphones crooked on her head. PHILIPPA ASHCROFT (30s, first-class passenger in a fur collar) stands behind her, gripping the back of the chair.

PHILIPPA
She said it was only a drill. She promised.

AGNES
She says a great many things, ma'am.

Philippa leans closer. Agnes pulls a sheet of paper from under the key and covers it with her sleeve. She watches her the way a cat watches a draft.

PHILIPPA
Show me what you wrote.

AGNES
I can't.

PHILIPPA
She told me to ask. She gave me leave.

The speaking tube whistles. Agnes snatches the cap off.

CAPTAIN HARGREAVES (V.O.)
(through the tube)
Miss Fenwick. Is the passenger with you?

AGNES
She is, sir.

CAPTAIN HARGREAVES (V.O.)
(through the tube)
Then you'll finish the message and you'll send it as written. All of it. Do you understand?

Philippa takes the paper from under Agnes's sleeve. She reads. Her face goes white. Agnes stands, and the chair scrapes the deck.

AGNES
Ma'am, please sit.

PHILIPPA
(very quiet)
Send it.

Agnes lowers her hand to the key. The spark leaps.
